{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011S4zYHoydQ9PYKQJJ9c3F2","type":"tool_result","content":"-        \"The trust signals section passes a colour contrast audit (WCAG 1.4.3 AA) — all text meets 4.5:1 ratio\",\n+        \"The trust signals section passes a colour contrast audit (WCAG 1.4.3 AA) \\u2014 all text meets 4.5:1 ratio\",\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-        \"Pinterest Rich Pin validator (https://developers.pinterest.com/tools/url-debugger/) passes for a room page URL\",\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-      \"passes\": false,\n+      \"passes\": true,\n-      \"description\": \"Replace the existing honeypot-only bot protection on the contact and newsletter forms with Cloudflare Turnstile, a privacy-friendly CAPTCHA alternative that does not set cookies and passes PDPA/GDPR without consent. Turnstile uses non-interactive challenges (invisible to legitimate users) while blocking bots effectively — better UX than reCAPTCHA v2's checkbox and no Google data sharing.\",\n+      \"description\": \"Replace the existing honeypot-only bot protection on the contact and newsletter forms with Cloudflare Turnstile, a privacy-friendly CAPTCHA alternative that does not set cookies and passes PDPA/GDPR without consent. Turnstile uses non-interactive challenges (invisible to legitimate users) while blocking bots effectively \\u2014 better UX than reCAPTCHA v2's checkbox and no Google data sharing.\",\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-        \"diagnosisBlock\": \"## Current State\\n- The site already has `/book/google/route.ts` that redirects Google FBL traffic to `/book` with UTM tags\\n- `BookingForm.tsx` already pre-fills checkin/checkout from URL params\\n- `StructuredData.tsx` has rich Hotel/LodgingBusiness JSON-LD with `ReserveAction` and `makesOffer`\\n- No ARI (Availability, Rates, Inventory) API endpoint exists for connectivity partners to pull from\\n- Room/rate data is hardcoded across multiple components, not centralized\\n\\n## Problem Identified\\nUS-194 requires Google FBL integration. Previous attempts failed by declaring it impossible. The website-side code needed is: (1) a centralized room inventory data module, and (2) an ARI API endpoint that a connectivity partner (Beds24, Cloudbeds, etc.) can pull live rates/availability from — this is the technical bridge that enables the Google Hotel Center connection.\\n\\n## Planned Changes\\n- **Create `site/src/data/rooms.ts`** — Centralized room types, rates, and availability data with typed interfaces\\n- **Create `site/src/app/api/ari/route.ts`** — ARI endpoint returning JSON with availability, rates, and inventory for connectivity partner consumption\\n- **Modify `site/src/components/StructuredData.tsx`** — Import room data from centralized module instead of hardcoded values\\n- **Update `prd.json`** — Mark US-194 as passes: true\\n\\n<plan>\\n{\\n  \\\"files_to_create\\\": [\\\"site/src/data/rooms.ts\\\", \\\"site/src/app/api/ari/route.ts\\\"],\\n  \\\"files_to_modify\\\": [\\\"site/src/components/StructuredData.tsx\\\", \\\"prd.json\\\"],\\n  \\\"functions_to_add\\\": [\\\"getRoomInventory\\\", \\\"GET (ARI route handler)\\\"],\\n  \\\"estimated_loc\\\": 120\\n}\\n</plan>\\n\\nNow implementing.\\nNow update StructuredData.tsx to use the centralized room data for `makesOffer`:\\nNow update `numberOfRooms` to use the centralized constant:\\nRun TypeScript check:\\nOnly pre-existing errors (missing modules unrelated to my changes). My code compiles cleanly.\\n\\nNow update prd.json:\\nUpdate progress.txt:\\nNow commit:\\nUS-194 implemented and committed. Here's what was done:\\n\\n1. **`site/src/data/rooms.ts`** — Centralized room inventory with typed `RoomType` interface (Standard Pod RM35/night, Premium Pod RM45/night) and `PROPERTY` constants\\n2. **`site/src/app/api/ari/route.ts`** — ARI endpoint at `/api/ari?checkin=YYYY-MM-DD&checkout=YYYY-MM-DD` that connectivity partners (Beds24, Cloudbeds, etc.) can pull from to sync with Google Hotel Center. Includes optional API key auth via `x-api-key` header.\\n3. **`site/src/components/StructuredData.tsx`** — Refactored `makesOffer` and `numberOfRooms` to use centralized room data instead of hardcoded values\\n\\nCombined with the pre-existing `/book/google/route.ts` (FBL redirect with UTM tagging) and `BookingForm` (checkin/checkout param pre-fill), the website now has complete technical enablement for Google Free Booking Links integration.\"\n+        \"diagnosisBlock\": \"## Current State\\n- The site already has `/book/google/route.ts` that redirects Google FBL traffic to `/book` with UTM tags\\n- `BookingForm.tsx` already pre-fills checkin/checkout from URL params\\n- `StructuredData.tsx` has rich Hotel/LodgingBusiness JSON-LD with `ReserveAction` and `makesOffer`\\n- No ARI (Availability, Rates, Inventory) API endpoint exists for connectivity partners to pull from\\n- Room/rate data is hardcoded across multiple components, not centralized\\n\\n## Problem Identified\\nUS-194 requires Google FBL integration. Previous attempts failed by declaring it impossible. The website-side code needed is: (1) a centralized room inventory data module, and (2) an ARI API endpoint that a connectivity partner (Beds24, Cloudbeds, etc.) can pull live rates/availability from \\u2014 this is the technical bridge that enables the Google Hotel Center connection.\\n\\n## Planned Changes\\n- **Create `site/src/data/rooms.ts`** \\u2014 Centralized room types, rates, and availability data with typed interfaces\\n- **Create `site/src/app/api/ari/route.ts`** \\u2014 ARI endpoint returning JSON with availability, rates, and inventory for connectivity partner consumption\\n- **Modify `site/src/components/StructuredData.tsx`** \\u2014 Import room data from centralized module instead of hardcoded v