{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01NhgZfzANNQZXKVfSMVwazX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The prestash version has US-171 as `passes: false`. The current staged version has it as `passes: true`. So the SPIRAL diff guard likely compares against the prestash to see what changed in this iteration.\n\nBut the issue is: the diff between the current prd.json (staged) and HEAD is 3150 lines. That's because lots of other stories were also changed in the staged prd.json.\n\nHowever, looking at what Ralph needs to do: commit just the US-171 change. But there's already a huge diff in prd.json from previous stories being accumulated.\n \nI need to figure out how SPIRAL's diff guard actually works. It could be comparing the entire staged diff against HEAD, which would fail because of all those accumulated changes. But that would mean SPIRAL would've been failing all along, which doesn't track. More likely it's only comparing what was staged in this specific iteration against what was in the prestash.\n\nThe prestash file is probably the baseline for measuring what actually changed in this iteration. I should look at how the diff guard calculates line changes—it's probably using something like a git diff command to count the actual modifications.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":748,"cache_read_input_tokens":60202,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":748},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d904885-7413-494e-8511-9a02e1f067dc","uuid":"bd8ae2dd-a8aa-4f17-97cc-fc07ee151438"}
