{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01K5srwe53z7XRPvEjgYQj69","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The SPIRAL_MAX_DIFF_LINES is set to 2000 in this project! Not 500 as the system prompt said. So the limit is 2000 lines. The previous attempt produced 7472 lines which exceeded even 2000.\n\nWith the current situation:\n- prd.json has 3150 lines of accumulated diff vs HEAD\n- progress.txt has some additions\n\nThis total is still over 2000 lines. But wait - does the diff guard run `git diff HEAD` or `git diff` (vs index) or something else?\n\n\nActually, I think the diff guard checks what's being committed in this iteration. If the staged changes include all the accumulated prd.json from previous iterations, the commit would include those 3150 lines. But SPIRAL iterations have been working fine across this project with many passed stories, so maybe I'm misunderstanding how the staged changes work. The git status shows `M prd.json` as staged, which is likely the accumulated changes SPIRAL has been collecting across multiple iterations before they get committed together. Let me reconsider how each iteration's commit actually works.\n\nLooking at the previous successful commit `192795f feat: Add Bing Webmaster Tools verification meta tag support` to understand what actually got included in that commit.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":179,"cache_read_input_tokens":61957,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":179},"output_tokens":30,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d904885-7413-494e-8511-9a02e1f067dc","uuid":"195833ca-8fc5-4deb-a19c-f09cff81d5b8"}
