{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012RLT3GPRE7s3Z9Y7jYoyq2","type":"tool_result","content":"commit d45ce3913b01353b9a4de85d538be38ccd9bd96a\nMerge: c1277d0 e4ba6ba\nAuthor: wenjyue84 <wenjyue@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Apr 14 06:05:55 2026 +0800\n\n    On master: spiral-auto-stash-iter-16\n\ndiff --cc prd.json\nindex 7c96828,e95e7b8..d96ee07\n--- a/prd.json\n+++ b/prd.json\n@@@ -3146,50 -3146,50 +3146,6 @@@\n        \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n        \"passes\": true\n      },\n--    {\n--      \"id\": \"US-143\",\n--      \"title\": \"Apply CSS @starting-style for GPU-accelerated entry animations\",\n--      \"priority\": \"low\",\n--      \"description\": \"CSS @starting-style (Baseline August 2024, supported in all major engines since Firefox 129) enables declarative entry animations for elements transitioning from display:none or entering the top layer without JavaScript. Room card reveals, modal dialogues, and the cookie consent banner can use @starting-style for smooth fade/slide-in animations that respect prefers-reduced-motion and require zero JavaScript.\",\n--      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n--        \"Room cards, modal overlays, and the cookie consent banner use @starting-style + transition instead of JavaScript-driven animation libraries for their entry animation\",\n--        \"All entry animations are paired with a @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) override that disables or minimises motion\",\n--        \"Animations use only transform and opacity to remain on the GPU compositor thread (no layout-triggering properties)\",\n--        \"Lighthouse Performance score does not regress (no new render-blocking resources introduced)\",\n--        \"Manual test in Firefox 129+, Chrome 125+, and Safari 17.4+ confirms animations render correctly\"\n--      ],\n--      \"technicalNotes\": [\n--        \"@starting-style MDN: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/At-rules/@starting-style\",\n--        \"Pair with transition-behavior: allow-discrete to animate discrete properties like display and visibility\",\n---\n prd.json | 822 ---------------------------------------------------------------\n 1 file changed, 822 deletions(-)\n[rerun: b55]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d904885-7413-494e-8511-9a02e1f067dc","uuid":"bf76cdbd-e2f4-4e0a-89aa-7f8eef0ec2bb","timestamp":"2026-04-13T22:19:10.973Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"commit d45ce3913b01353b9a4de85d538be38ccd9bd96a\nMerge: c1277d0 e4ba6ba\nAuthor: wenjyue84 <wenjyue@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Apr 14 06:05:55 2026 +0800\n\n    On master: spiral-auto-stash-iter-16\n\ndiff --cc prd.json\nindex 7c96828,e95e7b8..d96ee07\n--- a/prd.json\n+++ b/prd.json\n@@@ -3146,50 -3146,50 +3146,6 @@@\n        \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n        \"passes\": true\n      },\n--    {\n--      \"id\": \"US-143\",\n--      \"title\": \"Apply CSS @starting-style for GPU-accelerated entry animations\",\n--      \"priority\": \"low\",\n--      \"description\": \"CSS @starting-style (Baseline August 2024, supported in all major engines since Firefox 129) enables declarative entry animations for elements transitioning from display:none or entering the top layer without JavaScript. Room card reveals, modal dialogues, and the cookie consent banner can use @starting-style for smooth fade/slide-in animations that respect prefers-reduced-motion and require zero JavaScript.\",\n--      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n--        \"Room cards, modal overlays, and the cookie consent banner use @starting-style + transition instead of JavaScript-driven animation libraries for their entry animation\",\n--        \"All entry animations are paired with a @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) override that disables or minimises motion\",\n--        \"Animations use only transform and opacity to remain on the GPU compositor thread (no layout-triggering properties)\",\n--        \"Lighthouse Performance score does not regress (no new render-blocking resources introduced)\",\n--        \"Manual test in Firefox 129+, Chrome 125+, and Safari 17.4+ confirms animations render correctly\"\n--      ],\n--      \"technicalNotes\": [\n--        \"@starting-style MDN: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/At-rules/@starting-style\",\n--        \"Pair with transition-behavior: allow-discrete to animate discrete properties like display and visibility\",\n---\n prd.json | 822 ---------------------------------------------------------------\n 1 file changed, 822 deletions(-)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01XkxVb1DFq6wBaFXFy7UDEP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The auto-stash for iter-16 contains deletions of stories from prd.json (removing stories that were already handled). This is the stash that was created at the START of iter-16, capturing the working state before Ralph started.\n\nLooking at the structure:\n- The stash has 822 deletions from prd.json - these are stories being removed from the prd.json\n- The current staged prd.json has 3150 lines of diff vs HEAD\n\nThis means the current staged prd.json was already modified BEFORE this iteration started (before the auto-stash). \n\nThe 3150-line diff represents accumulated changes from multiple spiral iterations that never got committed. I'm trying to figure out what actually belongs in this commit—should I only include the prd.json change for US-171 (passes: false → true), like how the previous successful commit only had 8 lines changed when Ralph modified just US-081's passes field? The current state is unusual because prd.json has all these staged changes from before I started, which suggests cumulative drift across iterations.\n\nMy plan is to reset the staged prd.json back to HEAD, then make only the US-171 change using text replacement, and commit just that change along with progress.txt updates. This keeps the diff small and focused. But I'm second-guessing myself—if I reset prd.json, I'll lose the other staged changes like other stories being marked as passes=true, and those might actually be important. Then again, according to how SPIRAL is designed, I should only commit what's relevant to this specific story; the other changes from previous iterations will be handled by SPIRAL's orchestration separately.\n\nLet me trace back what happened with the auto-stash. The `_prd_prestash_16.json` file captures prd.json as it was at the start of iteration 16, and the current staged version has changes layered on top of HEAD. Those changes were already there before Ralph started working, since the auto-stash captured the working state at that moment. I need to check what HEAD was when the stash was created to understand the baseline.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1517,"cache_read_input_tokens":63090,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1517},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d904885-7413-494e-8511-9a02e1f067dc","uuid":"89567f83-ba3a-4725-9bde-9e1577d80e44"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01XkxVb1DFq6wBaFXFy7UDEP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K3AXgNzqSBaHyWJoFMgo24","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"C:/Users/Jyue/Documents/1-projects/Software Projects/pelangi-website\" && git diff HEAD -- prd.json | grep \"^[+-]\" | grep -v \"^---\\|^+++\" | grep \"passes\" | head -20","description":"Check all passes-related changes in staged prd.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1517,"cache_read_input_tokens":63090,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1517},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d904885-7413-494e-8511-9a02e1f067dc","uuid":"d767ece2-1935-4335-afdb-49352617bfb1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K3AXgNzqSBaHyWJoFMgo24","type":"tool_result","content":"-        \"The trust signals section passes a colour contrast audit (WCAG 1.4.3 AA) — all text meets 4.5:1 ratio\",\n+        \"The trust signals section passes a colour contrast audit (WCAG 1.4.3 AA) \\u2014 all text meets 4.5:1 ratio\",\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-        \"Pinterest Rich Pin validator (https://developers.pinterest.com/tools/url-debugger/) passes for a room page URL\",\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-      \"passes\": false,\n+      \"passes\": true,\n-      \"description\": \"Replace the existing honeypot-only bot protection on the contact and newsletter forms with Cloudflare Turnstile, a privacy-friendly CAPTCHA alternative that does not set cookies and passes PDPA/GDPR without consent. Turnstile uses non-interactive challenges (invisible to legitimate users) while blocking bots effectively — better UX than reCAPTCHA v2's checkbox and no Google data sharing.\",\n+      \"description\": \"Replace the existing honeypot-only bot protection on the contact and newsletter forms with Cloudflare Turnstile, a privacy-friendly CAPTCHA alternative that does not set cookies and passes PDPA/GDPR without consent. Turnstile uses non-interactive challenges (invisible to legitimate users) while blocking bots effectively \\u2014 better UX than reCAPTCHA v2's checkbox and no Google data sharing.\",\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-      \"passes\": false,\n-        \"diagnosisBlock\": \"## Current State\\n- The site already has `/book/google/route.ts` that redirects Google FBL traffic to `/book` with UTM tags\\n- `BookingForm.tsx` already pre-fills checkin/checkout from URL params\\n- `StructuredData.tsx` has rich Hotel/LodgingBusiness JSON-LD with `ReserveAction` and `makesOffer`\\n- No ARI (Availability, Rates, Inventory) API endpoint exists for connectivity partners to pull from\\n- Room/rate data is hardcoded across multiple components, not centralized\\n\\n## Problem Identified\\nUS-194 requires Google FBL integration. Previous attempts failed by declaring it impossible. The website-side code needed is: (1) a centralized room inventory data module, and (2) an ARI API endpoint that a connectivity partner (Beds24, Cloudbeds, etc.) can pull live rates/availability from — this is the technical bridge that enables the Google Hotel Center connection.\\n\\n## Planned Changes\\n- **Create `site/src/data/rooms.ts`** — Centralized room types, rates, and availability data with typed interfaces\\n- **Create `site/src/app/api/ari/route.ts`** — ARI endpoint returning JSON with availability, rates, and inventory for connectivity partner consumption\\n- **Modify `site/src/components/StructuredData.tsx`** — Import room data from centralized module instead of hardcoded values\\n- **Update `prd.json`** — Mark US-194 as passes: true\\n\\n<plan>\\n{\\n  \\\"files_to_create\\\": [\\\"site/src/data/rooms.ts\\\", \\\"site/src/app/api/ari/route.ts\\\"],\\n  \\\"files_to_modify\\\": [\\\"site/src/components/StructuredData.tsx\\\", \\\"prd.json\\\"],\\n  \\\"functions_to_add\\\": [\\\"getRoomInventory\\\", \\\"GET (ARI route handler)\\\"],\\n  \\\"estimated_loc\\\": 120\\n}\\n</plan>\\n\\nNow implementing.\\nNow update StructuredData.tsx to use the centralized room data for `makesOffer`:\\nNow update `numberOfRooms` to use the centralized constant:\\nRun TypeScript check:\\nOnly pre-existing errors (missing modules unrelated to my changes). My code compiles cleanly.\\n\\nNow update prd.json:\\nUpdate progress.txt:\\nNow commit:\\nUS-194 implemented and committed. Here's what was done:\\n\\n1. **`site/src/data/rooms.ts`** — Centralized room inventory with typed `RoomType` interface (Standard Pod RM35/night, Premium Pod RM45/night) and `PROPERTY` constants\\n2. **`site/src/app/api/ari/route.ts`** — ARI endpoint at `/api/ari?checkin=YYYY-MM-DD&checkout=YYYY-MM-DD` that connectivity partners (Beds24, Cloudbeds, etc.) can pull from to sync with Google Hotel Center. Includes optional API key auth via `x-api-key` header.\\n3. **`site/src/components/StructuredData.tsx`** — Refactored `makesOffer` and `numberOfRooms` to use centralized room data instead of hardcoded values\\n\\nCombined with the pre-existing `/book/google/route.ts` (FBL redirect with UTM tagging) and `BookingForm` (checkin/checkout param pre-fill), the website now has complete technical enablement for Google Free Booking Links integration.\"\n+        \"diagnosisBlock\": \"## Current State\\n- The site already has `/book/google/route.ts` that redirects Google FBL traffic to `/book` with UTM tags\\n- `BookingForm.tsx` already pre-fills checkin/checkout from URL params\\n- `StructuredData.tsx` has rich Hotel/LodgingBusiness JSON-LD with `ReserveAction` and `makesOffer`\\n- No ARI (Availability, Rates, Inventory) API endpoint exists for connectivity partners to pull from\\n- Room/rate data is hardcoded across multiple components, not centralized\\n\\n## Problem Identified\\nUS-194 requires Google FBL integration. Previous attempts failed by declaring it impossible. The website-side code needed is: (1) a centralized room inventory data module, and (2) an ARI API endpoint that a connectivity partner (Beds24, Cloudbeds, etc.) can pull live rates/availability from \\u2014 this is the technical bridge that enables the Google Hotel Center connection.\\n\\n## Planned Changes\\n- **Create `site/src/data/rooms.ts`** \\u2014 Centralized room types, rates, and availability data with typed interfaces\\n- **Create `site/src/app/api/ari/route.ts`** \\u2014 ARI endpoint returning JSON with availability, rates, and inventory for connectivity partner consumption\\n- **Modify `site/src/components/StructuredData.tsx`** \\u2014 Import room data from centralized module instead of hardcoded v